<title>ITALY: Italy's Prodi meets Ciampi to discuss accounts.</title>
<headline>Italy's Prodi meets Ciampi to discuss accounts.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi met Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi and Labour Minister Tiziano Treu on Tuesday to discuss state accounts, government sources said.</p>
<p>No further details of the meeting were available.</p>
<p>Prodi has said a decision on whether to pass a mini-budget for 1997 to help plug a deficit overshoot will be taken once official state accounts are finalised. That is expected to be early next month. ((   -- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501))</p>
</text>
